{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit built-in priors `sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100)` and `sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100)` for parameters that were already finitely constrained to `[0, 100]`. This makes the implicit bounded flat priors explicit so every parameter has exactly one SafeStan prior sampling statement before the protected likelihood. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> n_grade;
  int<lower=0> n_grade_pair;
  int<lower=0> n_pair;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_grade> grade;
  array[n_pair] int<lower=1, upper=n_grade_pair> grade_pair;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=n_pair> pair;
  vector[N] treatment;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[n_pair] eta_a;
  vector<lower=0, upper=100>[n_grade_pair] sigma_a;
  vector<lower=0, upper=100>[n_grade] sigma_y;
  vector[n_grade_pair] mu_a;
  vector[n_grade] b;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[n_pair] a;
  vector<lower=0>[N] sigma_y_hat;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : n_pair) {
    a[i] = 100 * mu_a[grade_pair[i]] + sigma_a[grade_pair[i]] * eta_a[i];
  }

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[pair[i]] + b[grade[i]] * treatment[i];
    sigma_y_hat[i] = sigma_y[grade[i]];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  b ~ normal(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y_hat);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":4,"grade":[1,1,2,2],"grade_pair":[1,1],"n_grade":2,"n_grade_pair":1,"n_pair":2,"pair":[1,1,1,2],"treatment":[3.3734620496586984,3.4207898221781243,4.308819400320084,6.522402372375893],"y":[4.0,3.0,4.0,2.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
